# ROWNAA — Phase 2: Customer Panel & Booking Flow

> This phase covers every screen a customer sees. Every field, every button, every state is explicitly defined. No placeholder forms.

---

## 1. Homepage Layout (Desktop)

### Section 1 — Sticky Navbar
- Logo (left): "ROWNAA" in `Outfit 700`, `var(--color-brand-accent)` color
- Nav links (center): Home | Services | How It Works | About | Contact
- Right side: `Login` button (ghost style) + `Sign Up` button (accent style)
- Background: `var(--color-brand-primary)` with `border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07)`
- Sticky on scroll: adds `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)` + glassmorphism background
- Height: `68px`

### Section 2 — Hero
- Full-width, height `90vh` minimum
- Background: `var(--gradient-hero)` with a subtle car silhouette image overlay (low opacity 15%)
- H1: "Book a car, anywhere you're headed." — `var(--text-hero)`, `var(--font-display)`
- Subtext: "6 services. Verified drivers. Your schedule." — `var(--text-h3)`, `var(--color-text-secondary)`
- Below subtext: Quick search bar (see Section 3 below)
- Floating stats below hero text (glassmorphism cards): "500+ Verified Cars" | "6 Services" | "Dhaka & Beyond"

### Section 3 — Quick Service Selector (Hero Embedded)
- A row of 6 icon-card tabs below the hero text
- Each card: Service icon (32px) + service name label
- Selected state: card gets `var(--color-brand-accent)` border + background tint
- Clicking a card = scrolls to / reveals the booking form for that service

### Section 4 — How It Works
- 3-column layout: "Choose Service" → "Book & Pay 20%" → "Driver Comes to You"
- Each step: numbered circle icon + heading + 2-line description

### Section 5 — Service Showcase Cards
- Grid: 3 columns × 2 rows = 6 cards
- Each card: background image (dark overlay), service name, 1-line description, "Book Now" button
- Services: Airport Transfer | Corporate | Car Rental | Intercity | Travel & Tour | Event & Wedding

### Section 6 — Footer
- Logo + tagline | Service links | Contact (phone, email) | Social media icons
- Dark background matching brand primary
- Copyright line at bottom

---

## 2. Auth Pages

### Login Page
- Centered card on `var(--gradient-hero)` background
- Title: "Welcome back"
- Field 1: Phone number input (auto-formats as user types)
- OR divider
- Field 2: Email input (alternative)
- Password field (if email login)
- "Send OTP" button (if phone) — triggers SMS OTP
- OTP input: 4-digit boxes (separate inputs, auto-tab between them)
- "Verify & Login" button
- Link: "New here? Register" | "Are you a car owner? Register your vehicle"

### Register Page (Customer)
- Name, Phone, Email (optional), Password
- OTP verification step after form submit
- After verification → redirect to homepage

---

## 3. The 6 Booking Forms

**Layout Rule:** When a service card is clicked on the homepage, a full-page booking form appears. The form has two parts:
- **Part A:** Common fields (always visible)
- **Part B:** Service-specific fields (change based on service)

All forms must have a sticky "Book Now" button at the bottom that stays visible as user scrolls.

---

### Common Fields (Part A) — present on ALL 6 services

| Field | Type | Validation |
|---|---|---|
| Full Name | Text input | Required, min 3 chars |
| Mobile Number | Tel input with +880 prefix | Required, exactly 11 digits |
| Pickup Location | Structured dropdown (Google Places area select) | Required — NEVER free text |
| Pickup Date | Date picker — no past dates | Required |
| Pickup Time | Time picker (15-min intervals) | Required |
| Car Type Preference | Segmented buttons: Sedan / SUV / Microbus / Noah-Hiace / Any | Default = "Any" |
| Number of Passengers | Number stepper (+/- buttons) min=1 | Required for seat matching |
| Special Note | Textarea, max 300 chars | Optional |

---

### Service 01 — Car Rental with Hourly (service_data JSONB)

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Rental Mode | Toggle: "Hourly" / "Daily" | Changes the next fields |
| Start Date & Time | DateTime picker | Required |
| End Date & Time | DateTime picker OR "I'll estimate" checkbox | Required (or estimated flag set) |
| Estimated Duration | Auto-calculated from start/end, shown as "X hours / Y days" | Read-only display |
| Trip Scope | Toggle: "Within City" / "Outside City" | Affects pricing guidance |

**UI Behavior:** Selecting "I'll estimate" on end time hides the end date picker and shows a duration input (hours stepper). Selecting "Outside City" shows an additional destination area dropdown.

---

### Service 02 — Airport Transfer (service_data JSONB)

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Pickup Direction | Toggle: "FROM Airport" / "TO Airport" | Changes next fields |
| Airport Name | Dropdown: Hazrat Shahjalal / Shah Amanat / Osmani / Other | Required |
| Trip Type | Toggle: "One-way" / "Round Trip" | |
| Drop Location | Structured area dropdown (appears if "From Airport") | Required if from airport |
| Pickup Location (alternate) | Structured area dropdown (appears if "To Airport") | Common field merges here |
| Return Date & Time | DateTime picker | Appears ONLY if Round Trip |
| Flight Details | Text input (optional) — "PG101 arriving 3PM" | Optional, for driver planning |

**UI Behavior:** The "FROM Airport" vs "TO Airport" toggle dynamically swaps which location field is labeled "Pickup" vs "Drop". The common Pickup Location field from Part A relabels itself accordingly.

---

### Service 03 — Intercity Travel (service_data JSONB)

> **CRITICAL NOTE:** This is NOT the same as Travel & Tour. Intercity = one city to another, point-to-point, no multi-day itinerary.

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| From City | Dropdown (list of cities) | Required |
| To City | Dropdown (list of cities) | Required, must differ from From |
| Trip Type | Toggle: "One-way" / "Round Trip" | |
| Return Date & Time | DateTime picker | Appears ONLY if Round Trip |
| Preferred Pickup Point | Text/area input within the origin city | Required |
| Drop Point | Text/area input within the destination city | Required |

---

### Service 04 — Travel & Tour (service_data JSONB)

> **CRITICAL NOTE:** This is NOT Intercity. Tour = multi-destination, multi-day package with itinerary.

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| From City | Dropdown | Required |
| Destination(s) | Multi-select tag input (add multiple cities) | Required, min 1 destination |
| Trip Type | Toggle: "One-way" / "Round Trip" | |
| Trip Duration | Number stepper (days) min=1 | Required |
| Itinerary Detail | Large textarea "List places you want to visit" | Optional |

---

### Service 05 — Event & Wedding Transport (service_data JSONB)

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Event Type | Dropdown: Wedding / Family Function / Corporate Event / Other | Required |
| Event Date | Date picker | Required, must be future |
| Venue Location | Structured area dropdown | Required |
| Duration | Number stepper (hours) min=1 | Required |
| Multiple Cars? | Toggle: "Yes" / "No" | Default = No |
| Number of Cars | Number stepper (appears ONLY if Multiple = Yes) | Min=2 |
| Guest Count | Number input (optional, helps suggest car count) | Optional |

**UI Behavior:** When "Multiple Cars = Yes" is selected, the Number of Cars stepper fades in. If Guest Count is entered, the system shows a suggestion: "Suggested: 2 cars based on guest count."

---

### Service 06 — Corporate Transport (service_data JSONB)

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Company Name | Text input | Required |
| Office Pickup Point | Structured area dropdown | Required |
| Drop Location | Structured area dropdown | Required |
| Booking Type | Toggle: "One-time" / "Recurring" | Default = One-time |
| Recurring Frequency | Dropdown: Daily / Weekly / Monthly (appears if Recurring) | Required if recurring |
| Number of Days | Number stepper (appears if Recurring) | Required if recurring |
| Which Days | Multi-checkbox: Mon/Tue/Wed/Thu/Fri/Sat/Sun (appears if Weekly) | Required if weekly |
| Number of Passengers | Number stepper min=1 | Required |

